# Not an optimisation — the Dockerfile COPYs files by name and src/ only. It is
# a guard: the day a `COPY . .` appears, or a `.env` or a local `dist/` is
# sitting in the working directory when the release workflow runs, this is what
# keeps it out of an image that gets pushed to two registries.
node_modules/
dist/
.git/
.github/
.env*
*.log
